WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:20.639 --> 00:00:23.996
GRAB SUN JAE AND RUN

2
00:00:26.474 --> 00:00:28.791
EPISODE 7

3
00:00:33.147 --> 00:00:34.505
No matter how I look, she is sleeping.

4
00:00:45.415 --> 00:00:46.693
It's time to go out.

5
00:00:48.172 --> 00:00:49.172
Salt.

6
00:00:55.445 --> 00:00:56.883
Salt, it's time to go out.

7
00:01:32.128 --> 00:01:34.126
- Yes.
- Haven’t woken up yet?

8
00:01:34.446 --> 00:01:37.163
If this is the case, go to the end!

9
00:01:37.243 --> 00:01:40.559
Pretend you missed it too
stop and come back together!

10
00:01:41.399 --> 00:01:43.756
At least talk to her this time, you fool!

11
00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:45.395
That's all for now. We need to wake her up.

12
00:02:21.958 --> 00:02:22.958
What?

13
00:02:23.197 --> 00:02:24.316
When did she have time?

14
00:02:26.034 --> 00:02:28.192
Driver! Stop, please!

15
00:02:28.272 --> 00:02:29.471
I can't!

16
00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:31.828
The stop is close, you can get off there.

17
00:02:32.188 --> 00:02:33.706
But I need it here!

18
00:02:37.463 --> 00:02:39.900
Damn it. The bus won't arrive?

19
00:02:45.135 --> 00:02:46.613
Call your mom, or what?

20
00:02:54.805 --> 00:02:55.805
Taxi!

21
00:03:06.993 --> 00:03:08.591
- Are you sitting down?
- What?

22
00:03:11.029 --> 00:03:12.029
Oh...

23
00:03:12.787 --> 00:03:15.544
Mom said she would pick me up.
Sorry.

24
00:03:15.624 --> 00:03:16.624
Well, okay.

25
00:03:53.626 --> 00:03:54.626
Already left.

26
00:04:27.552 --> 00:04:29.191
Yes, the bus won't come.

27
00:04:31.788 --> 00:04:33.107
I'll catch a taxi.

28
00:05:34.685 --> 00:05:36.643
Crap. I managed to escape.

29
00:06:41.179 --> 00:06:42.179
Salt!

30
00:06:44.296 --> 00:06:45.296
Lim Sol!

31
00:07:22.018 --> 00:07:23.018
No.

32
00:07:53.387 --> 00:07:54.387
Salt.

33
00:08:02.218 --> 00:08:03.218
Sorry.

34
00:08:03.976 --> 00:08:04.976
Salt.

35
00:08:08.931 --> 00:08:09.931
Where?!

36
00:08:16.004 --> 00:08:17.004
Freak!

37
00:08:23.596 --> 00:08:24.596
Crap!

38
00:08:26.114 --> 00:08:27.114
Here you go!

39
00:08:28.072 --> 00:08:29.151
Gotcha.

40
00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:30.590
Lie down.

41
00:08:32.667 --> 00:08:33.667
Lie down, puppy.

42
00:08:36.144 --> 00:08:37.144
Crap.

43
00:08:43.497 --> 00:08:44.497
Crap!

44
00:08:45.894 --> 00:08:48.132
Let me go! Back off.

45
00:08:55.964 --> 00:08:56.964
Crap.

46
00:08:57.562 --> 00:08:58.562
Lie!

47
00:08:59.001 --> 00:09:01.039
- Don't move!
- Hold him!

48
00:09:01.279 --> 00:09:04.755
No no! Let me in! Let me go, bastards!

49
00:09:06.034 --> 00:09:08.591
Freaks. Let me in.

50
00:09:23.816 --> 00:09:26.573
SEPTEMBER 1, 2008

51
00:09:28.571 --> 00:09:30.609
DAY OF THE ACCIDENT

52
00:09:30.689 --> 00:09:33.407
Lim Sol! I asked him to bring the charger!

53
00:09:34.126 --> 00:09:36.124
I mean... Where is she?

54
00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:22.078
It wasn't an accident.

55
00:10:55.844 --> 00:10:56.844
What's here...

56
00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:11.150
Don't scare me like that!

57
00:11:12.947 --> 00:11:13.947
My friend!

58
00:11:14.705 --> 00:11:17.622
-Where are you going?
- Is Sol at home now?

59
00:11:17.702 --> 00:11:18.702
No.

60
00:11:19.141 --> 00:11:21.538
Here is a sheep, she said,
that he will stay at home.

61
00:11:21.618 --> 00:11:22.657
Where did she go?

62
00:11:23.097 --> 00:11:24.975
- Will he stay at home?
- Yes.

63
00:11:25.375 --> 00:11:28.012
She shouted that she couldn’t go out.

64
00:11:28.332 --> 00:11:31.129
And a couple of days ago I asked
break her legs

65
00:11:31.209 --> 00:11:34.925
if he suddenly says that he is going to go
to the reservoir.

66
00:11:35.245 --> 00:11:36.245
Reservoir?

67
00:11:38.881 --> 00:11:40.040
What are we going to do?

68
00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:41.678
He took your phone.

69
00:11:44.076 --> 00:11:47.033
- What's happened?
- I remembered how I got into an accident.

70
00:11:47.113 --> 00:11:48.991
The one you were talking about?

71
00:11:49.471 --> 00:11:51.029
Did this happen here?

72
00:11:51.269 --> 00:11:53.387
Yes. It turns out so.

73
00:11:53.906 --> 00:11:57.902
To the reservoir where she once was
got into an accident?

74
00:11:57.982 --> 00:11:59.021
In an accident?

75
00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:02.258
What other accident, not a scratch on it.

76
00:12:02.617 --> 00:12:03.976
Were there any accidents?

77
00:12:04.056 --> 00:12:06.054
And what? Did something happen to her?

78
00:12:07.293 --> 00:12:11.009
Wait. She seemed to be dreaming
how she was shot down at the reservoir.

79
00:12:11.089 --> 00:12:13.247
Nightmare. I had a nightmare.

80
00:12:13.327 --> 00:12:15.524
I dreamed that you were hurt
at the competition.

81
00:12:15.604 --> 00:12:17.283
It was like reality.

82
00:12:20.759 --> 00:12:21.759
What's wrong with him?

83
00:12:58.082 --> 00:13:00.040
Exactly. I can run away.

84
00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:01.798
I've been here before.

85
00:13:01.958 --> 00:13:03.317
I'll change fate.

86
00:13:44.276 --> 00:13:47.632
JUYANG RESERVOIR
FISHING IS PROHIBITED

87
00:14:44.935 --> 00:14:47.932
Damn it. Damn her.

88
00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:24.575
That is, the person disappeared, and for some reason you
decided to come here?

89
00:15:24.655 --> 00:15:26.813
Yes? I understand that your instinct led you, right?

90
00:15:26.893 --> 00:15:28.891
Can you just look for it?

91
00:15:29.291 --> 00:15:30.729
God help me.

92
00:15:30.809 --> 00:15:33.367
It's because here
killed a person?

93
00:15:33.447 --> 00:15:36.523
What makes you all think that something
should happen?

94
00:15:36.603 --> 00:15:40.200
I bet she's either in a karaoke bar,
or in an internet cafe now.

95
00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:41.280
Just...

96
00:15:53.387 --> 00:15:55.145
There's a reservoir there.

97
00:15:56.464 --> 00:15:57.464
So...

98
00:15:59.301 --> 00:16:00.500
What to do?

99
00:16:00.579 --> 00:16:02.537
And today is September 1st?

100
00:16:02.617 --> 00:16:05.894
That schoolgirl was afraid
that something will happen to her.

101
00:16:08.252 --> 00:16:09.252
What?

102
00:16:54.965 --> 00:16:56.883
Salt! Lim Sol!

103
00:17:03.397 --> 00:17:05.634
I just have to come to terms with it.

104
00:17:07.992 --> 00:17:11.069
It's a fate you can't escape.

105
00:17:21.179 --> 00:17:22.179
Salt!

106
00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:31.089
-Are you okay?
- Yes.

107
00:17:31.169 --> 00:17:32.647
Girl, how are you?

108
00:17:34.406 --> 00:17:35.684
I was saved.

109
00:17:48.631 --> 00:17:49.870
Where am I?

110
00:17:51.508 --> 00:17:52.508
Salt...

111
00:17:53.147 --> 00:17:54.147
...are you okay?

112
00:18:03.097 --> 00:18:04.535
What happened to you?

113
00:18:07.572 --> 00:18:09.371
Where are we now?

114
00:18:13.287 --> 00:18:15.445
Who are you?

115
00:18:18.881 --> 00:18:22.118
- Lim Sol!
- That night with my lips...

116
00:18:23.077 --> 00:18:24.835
did you take possession? Tell.

117
00:18:24.915 --> 00:18:26.074
No, sir!

118
00:18:26.234 --> 00:18:30.829
Your humble maid is simply
stumbled and fell.

119
00:18:31.189 --> 00:18:33.307
Your Highness, I didn't know.

120
00:18:33.387 --> 00:18:35.544
What? This...

121
00:18:36.224 --> 00:18:39.421
How can this be? You can't stay in debt.

122
00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:40.819
Joseon?

123
00:18:46.054 --> 00:18:47.213
Can't be.

124
00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:51.848
Nooo!

125
00:18:51.928 --> 00:18:52.928
Cut!

126
00:18:53.047 --> 00:18:54.525
What do you mean, "no"?

127
00:18:54.685 --> 00:18:57.323
Director Cho! What are you even doing?

128
00:18:57.403 --> 00:19:00.519
I'm sorry! Let's take a break for 10 minutes!

129
00:19:00.599 --> 00:19:03.516
- Almost taken off, what is it?
- That's it.

130
00:19:03.596 --> 00:19:04.875
What's here...

131
00:19:07.712 --> 00:19:10.030
You work with films yourself.

132
00:19:10.549 --> 00:19:12.707
The year has just begun and we are late.

133
00:19:14.985 --> 00:19:18.901
JANUARY 1, 2023, SUNDAY
It's 2023, right? We're not in Joseon?

134
00:19:18.981 --> 00:19:21.778
- What?
- God, I survived.

135
00:19:23.576 --> 00:19:25.614
Survived. Survived.

136
00:19:26.014 --> 00:19:28.731
What? She's kind of sick.

137
00:19:30.769 --> 00:19:33.247
What? Who does he call sick?

138
00:19:33.886 --> 00:19:35.924
Salt, it's cold! Here, put it on.

139
00:19:36.444 --> 00:19:37.522
And zip up.

140
00:19:38.402 --> 00:19:39.402
Lim Sol!

141
00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:40.680
Are you crying?

142
00:19:42.637 --> 00:19:45.275
Because of this idiot? Come on.

143
00:19:45.355 --> 00:19:47.952
We changed at the last minute
storyboard,

144
00:19:48.032 --> 00:19:50.829
found extras,
and he didn’t say “thank you”?

145
00:19:50.909 --> 00:19:54.865
Since he needs a good game,
let him hire actors!

146
00:19:54.985 --> 00:19:55.985
Right?

147
00:19:56.464 --> 00:19:57.464
Sorry.

148
00:19:57.982 --> 00:20:00.539
- And you...
- What do you mean? Who?

149
00:20:01.538 --> 00:20:02.538
I?

150
00:20:05.734 --> 00:20:06.973
How can I help?

151
00:20:08.851 --> 00:20:10.569
Nice to meet you!

152
00:20:13.766 --> 00:20:15.325
I changed fate!

153
00:20:18.841 --> 00:20:19.841
What's happened?

154
00:20:23.796 --> 00:20:25.155
Saved him.

155
00:20:30.749 --> 00:20:31.749
Salt!

156
00:20:33.946 --> 00:20:34.946
What about Sung Jae?

157
00:20:41.978 --> 00:20:44.096
RYU SUN JAE

158
00:20:47.932 --> 00:20:51.089
RYU SUN JAE

159
00:20:59.281 --> 00:21:00.999
RYU SUN JAE, SINGER

160
00:21:10.509 --> 00:21:12.148
Thank you, Sung Jae.

161
00:21:23.896 --> 00:21:29.850
January 1, 2023. At midnight.
Near the Han River. Understood?

162
00:21:42.797 --> 00:21:46.114
HAN RIVER

163
00:21:55.624 --> 00:21:56.663
Am I late?

164
00:21:58.382 --> 00:22:00.020
He didn't go alone, did he?

165
00:22:12.488 --> 00:22:15.045
I mean... Where's the tree?

166
00:22:39.461 --> 00:22:40.699
Song Jae.

167
00:23:59.900 --> 00:24:00.979
How long have you been here?

168
00:24:01.658 --> 00:24:02.697
I was waiting for the call.

169
00:24:07.133 --> 00:24:08.133
Jerk.

170
00:24:11.369 --> 00:24:13.606
What is this, a public bath?

171
00:24:13.966 --> 00:24:15.325
Have you come to wash yourself?

172
00:24:15.405 --> 00:24:18.402
You have a cool bathroom.
And a view of the city at night.

173
00:24:19.081 --> 00:24:20.519
Listen, I'll pay.

174
00:24:21.239 --> 00:24:22.239
Will you let me stay?

175
00:24:22.398 --> 00:24:24.036
I'll give you a minute. Get out.

176
00:24:26.673 --> 00:24:27.673
Me too.

177
00:24:36.224 --> 00:24:37.224
What's happened?

178
00:24:46.653 --> 00:24:47.653
Who's there?

179
00:24:56.164 --> 00:24:57.164
Young woman!

180
00:24:58.561 --> 00:24:59.561
Sorry.

181
00:25:01.678 --> 00:25:02.877
- Stop!
- What?

182
00:25:03.357 --> 00:25:04.595
Her again?

183
00:25:06.234 --> 00:25:07.393
I'm calling the police.

184
00:25:18.581 --> 00:25:20.819
God! Wait, you...

185
00:25:21.698 --> 00:25:22.698
dropped...

186
00:25:23.257 --> 00:25:26.134
TAKE SUN JAE AND RUN
Wow! Sung Jae fan?

187
00:25:26.853 --> 00:25:28.172
Take it and run.

188
00:25:28.332 --> 00:25:29.930
- Sorry! You...
- Caught!

189
00:25:30.969 --> 00:25:31.969
What?

190
00:25:33.327 --> 00:25:34.805
- Here! Here!
- What?

191
00:25:35.365 --> 00:25:36.643
We came to the call.

192
00:25:36.723 --> 00:25:37.842
I caught her!

193
00:25:38.242 --> 00:25:39.242
What?

194
00:25:40.320 --> 00:25:42.358
Be quiet, be quiet!

195
00:25:42.478 --> 00:25:46.314
- Yes, I understand you.
- We don't do that...

196
00:25:47.672 --> 00:25:49.471
Thank you for staying alive.

197
00:25:50.430 --> 00:25:51.628
First name, last name?

198
00:25:57.063 --> 00:25:58.063
Young woman.

199
00:26:00.180 --> 00:26:01.658
Handsome, tell me?

200
00:26:01.738 --> 00:26:02.937
A difficult case.

201
00:26:03.856 --> 00:26:04.856
Young woman!

202
00:26:05.335 --> 00:26:06.335
Name?

203
00:26:07.053 --> 00:26:08.053
Name!

204
00:26:08.731 --> 00:26:10.330
- What?
- Name.

205
00:26:11.489 --> 00:26:12.489
Yes.

206
00:26:14.046 --> 00:26:16.364
- Lim Sol.
- Your ID.

207
00:26:24.036 --> 00:26:25.435
Where do you work?

208
00:26:27.592 --> 00:26:28.671
In the company.

209
00:26:29.111 --> 00:26:32.308
I opened my eyes and found out
that I work in a film studio!

210
00:26:32.388 --> 00:26:35.345
You know, I've always dreamed
become a director.

211
00:26:36.024 --> 00:26:37.423
How amazing!

212
00:26:37.502 --> 00:26:41.019
One decision can change
all future fate.

213
00:26:41.099 --> 00:26:44.535
From a life where you can't dream,
straight into your dream life!

214
00:26:44.895 --> 00:26:48.531
Any destiny can be changed,
if you want, right?

215
00:26:48.611 --> 00:26:52.208
If this fate - there is only one
prison stew

216
00:26:52.288 --> 00:26:53.526
then I doubt it.

217
00:26:54.725 --> 00:26:59.321
Penetration into a home entails
criminal liability.

218
00:26:59.680 --> 00:27:02.717
Think about the evidence. Fine?

219
00:27:02.797 --> 00:27:04.276
Above the testimony?

220
00:27:04.795 --> 00:27:08.112
Here's how. Just stand
Is it illegal for expensive apartments?

221
00:27:08.192 --> 00:27:09.351
Just stand.

222
00:27:10.030 --> 00:27:12.867
You almost opened the door
Ryu Sung Jae's apartment.

223
00:27:12.947 --> 00:27:14.625
How do you know the password?

224
00:27:14.705 --> 00:27:17.942
What? Who had the conscience to do such a thing?

225
00:27:18.022 --> 00:27:20.939
Is this a maniac? Crazy?
What kind of piece of garbage is this?

226
00:27:21.019 --> 00:27:22.577
It turns out it's you.

227
00:27:22.657 --> 00:27:26.014
- I’m telling you, not me!
- This crazy woman is you, lady.

228
00:27:26.094 --> 00:27:27.852
- Once again...
- If the identity is established,

229
00:27:27.932 --> 00:27:29.291
let her go.

230
00:27:29.371 --> 00:27:34.006
The victim will not write a statement.
Doesn't want to make a fuss.

231
00:27:35.125 --> 00:27:37.443
Me too. It turns out you're lucky.

232
00:27:37.522 --> 00:27:40.879
Why won't he write a statement?
You can't let them go!

233
00:27:40.959 --> 00:27:44.875
They need to be caught and imprisoned! My God.
He hasn't changed at all.

234
00:27:44.955 --> 00:27:46.953
So kind and spineless!

235
00:27:48.112 --> 00:27:50.070
Can I write a statement?

236
00:27:50.150 --> 00:27:52.867
Yes, Sung Jae. I said we won't
write a statement.

237
00:27:52.947 --> 00:27:54.545
We don't need articles.

238
00:27:54.625 --> 00:27:57.702
- Yes, bye.
- Why don’t you accept the application?

239
00:27:57.782 --> 00:27:59.700
- Girl, go.
- No, wait.

240
00:27:59.780 --> 00:28:01.219
- It is forbidden!
- Wait.

241
00:28:01.698 --> 00:28:04.535
- Why?
- Here she is, in a white jacket.

242
00:28:04.655 --> 00:28:07.133
She looks normal, but no, she’s crazy.

243
00:28:07.772 --> 00:28:09.690
By the way, I saw it somewhere.

244
00:28:10.490 --> 00:28:11.768
We need to punish her.

245
00:28:12.527 --> 00:28:14.885
Let it be a lesson for everyone else too.

246
00:28:19.121 --> 00:28:21.878
- What is this?
- If you've had a swim, leave.

247
00:28:25.794 --> 00:28:27.632
Do you think I came for a swim?

248
00:28:28.392 --> 00:28:30.110
You refused to act.

249
00:28:30.190 --> 00:28:32.907
The CEO is tearing up and rushing about, Sung Jae.

250
00:28:32.987 --> 00:28:35.065
He asks to talk to you, to convince you.

251
00:28:35.904 --> 00:28:38.501
Read it yourself. Can you convince?

252
00:28:39.261 --> 00:28:40.939
You're picky.

253
00:28:42.697 --> 00:28:45.335
"HERO"
Well, hero! That's enough!

254
00:28:46.054 --> 00:28:47.652
A film about a hero, then?

255
00:28:48.412 --> 00:28:49.730
Yes, sure.

256
00:28:50.769 --> 00:28:52.887
No? And about whom?

257
00:28:53.127 --> 00:28:57.203
Mermaid swims across the Imjingan River
and meets a North Korean officer.

258
00:28:57.283 --> 00:28:58.283
And falls in love!

259
00:28:58.362 --> 00:29:00.679
Suddenly the zombie virus spreads.

260
00:29:00.759 --> 00:29:03.317
The mermaid and the officer kill the zombies.

261
00:29:03.636 --> 00:29:04.715
So this is an action blockbuster!

262
00:29:04.795 --> 00:29:06.074
Science fiction.

263
00:29:06.154 --> 00:29:07.473
The officer turned out...

264
00:29:08.192 --> 00:29:11.069
- ...an alien.
- Does the story continue in space?

265
00:29:11.588 --> 00:29:16.663
Song Jae! Song Jae! Song Jae! That girl!
That abnormal one... She, she...

266
00:29:18.302 --> 00:29:21.259
- What again?
- She... No, I'm suffocating.

267
00:29:21.778 --> 00:29:23.097
She's a psychopath.

268
00:29:23.896 --> 00:29:26.733
Why? Organized a concert
right at the station?

269
00:29:29.011 --> 00:29:30.450
Move over.

270
00:29:31.489 --> 00:29:32.727
I'm not sure...

271
00:29:34.725 --> 00:29:38.282
but it seems she works in this studio.

272
